            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0135" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/9212: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-20T15:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 22—2:29
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>88. Department’s 261, December 31, 5 p.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d42-f1"/> I am
                    today in receipt of a formal appeal from Minister for Foreign Affairs that the
                    United <pb facs="0136" n="38" xml:id="pg38"/> States assign an American
                    representative to the plebiscite commission at Teschen.</p>
                <p>In view of the Department’s telegram and of the confidence which would be
                    inspired here by such an appointment I trust the Department will see its way to
                    meet the wishes of the Polish Government. As the plebiscite may take place in a
                    short time the Department may desire to assign some one now in Europe.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
